{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/manga-from-old-picture-scrolls-to-new-global-hits/audio/main-9d79b49b88a1.mp3","durationSec":269.808,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":2.7,"text":"These old works are manga's early illustrated roots."},{"start":2.7,"end":5.24,"text":"Manga has very old roots in Japan."},{"start":6.08,"end":10.56,"text":"Around the year 1200, artists drew funny animal pictures on long paper scrolls."},{"start":11.22,"end":16.34,"text":"These scrolls are called Chōjū-giga, which means 'animal caricatures.'"},{"start":17.54,"end":19.68,"text":"Frogs and rabbits wrestle and play like humans."},{"start":20.38,"end":23.12,"text":"Many people call Chōjū-giga the oldest manga."},{"start":24.6,"end":31.08,"text":"About 600 years later, an artist named Katsushika Hokusai used the word 'manga' for the first time."},{"start":31.88,"end":36.3,"text":"In 1814, he published a book of sketches called Hokusai Manga."},{"start":37.14,"end":40.36,"text":"The book showed people, animals, plants, and landscapes."},{"start":41.28,"end":45.32,"text":"Hokusai drew over 3,000 pictures across 15 volumes."},{"start":45.92,"end":49.5,"text":"His work showed that a series of pictures could tell many ideas together."},{"start":50.5,"end":53.76,"text":"This modern manga development changed picture stories in Japan."},{"start":54.74,"end":56.72,"text":"Modern manga began after World War Two."},{"start":56.72,"end":62.12,"text":"American comic books came to Japan, and Japanese artists saw a new way to tell stories."},{"start":62.96,"end":64.66,"text":"One young artist changed everything."},{"start":65.88,"end":69.14,"text":"Osamu Tezuka published New Treasure Island in 1947."},{"start":70.46,"end":76.76,"text":"This comic book told an adventure story with fast camera-like angles, close-up faces, and action scenes."},{"start":77.84,"end":78.98,"text":"Young readers loved it."},{"start":79.5,"end":81.72,"text":"About 400,000 copies sold quickly."},{"start":82.58,"end":84.4,"text":"Many other artists copied Tezuka's style."},{"start":85.06,"end":90.08,"text":"He later created Astro Boy, a story about a robot boy, which also became a famous anime."},{"start":91.34,"end":93.52,"text":"Tezuka is often called 'the God of Manga.'"},{"start":94.84,"end":98.16,"text":"His work set the visual style that most people think of as manga today."},{"start":98.9,"end":102.36,"text":"New kinds of stories helped manga reach wide manga audiences."},{"start":103.42,"end":105.06,"text":"Not everyone wants the same story."},{"start":105.06,"end":109.06,"text":"Manga publishers learned this and made different types for different readers."},{"start":109.64,"end":114.48,"text":"In the 1950s and 1960s, some artists wanted more serious stories for adults."},{"start":115.34,"end":119.12,"text":"They created a style called gekiga, which means 'dramatic pictures.'"},{"start":119.12,"end":123.72,"text":"Gekiga stories showed real life problems, crime, and social issues."},{"start":124.6,"end":127.62,"text":"At the same time, publishers started making manga for girls."},{"start":128.26,"end":130.24,"text":"This type is called shōjo manga."},{"start":130.24,"end":134.2,"text":"Shōjo stories focused on feelings, friendships, and romance."},{"start":135.1,"end":138.08,"text":"The pictures used large expressive eyes and soft lines."},{"start":139.04,"end":143.24,"text":"Today, there is manga for children, teenagers, men, women, and older adults."},{"start":143.82,"end":146.1,"text":"Each type has its own name and its own magazine."},{"start":147.32,"end":152.42,"text":"This is one reason why manga became so popular — almost everyone can find a story made for them."},{"start":153.4,"end":156.7,"text":"Official online services now give manga global digital reach."},{"start":156.7,"end":162.4,"text":"Manga moved from Japan to the whole world, first through anime and then through digital technology."},{"start":162.82,"end":169.08,"text":"When Astro Boy became a TV anime in 1963, international audiences discovered Tezuka's characters."},{"start":169.76,"end":171.16,"text":"Other manga titles followed."},{"start":171.16,"end":178,"text":"Later, publishers began translating manga into English, French, Spanish, and many other languages."},{"start":179,"end":182.1,"text":"Now readers can use digital platforms to read manga online."},{"start":183.22,"end":187.24,"text":"Some publishers release new chapters at the same time in Japan and in other countries."},{"start":188.06,"end":190.18,"text":"This is called a simultaneous release."},{"start":191.62,"end":199,"text":"KADOKAWA, one of Japan's biggest manga publishers, offers simultaneous English digital chapter releases through its services."},{"start":200.08,"end":204.52,"text":"Readers anywhere in the world can follow their favourite story the same week it comes out in Japan."},{"start":204.52,"end":209.18,"text":"Manga publishing with visual language keeps a story moving."},{"start":209.18,"end":213.5,"text":"Manga uses special pictures and publishing tools to keep readers excited."},{"start":214.5,"end":216.78,"text":"One important visual tool is speed lines."},{"start":217.36,"end":220.78,"text":"These are thin lines drawn around a moving object or a character's face."},{"start":220.78,"end":228.68,"text":"Researchers studied speed lines and found that they make readers feel movement and direction, even in a still picture."},{"start":229.48,"end":231.32,"text":"A punch with speed lines feels fast."},{"start":232.1,"end":233.8,"text":"A running character feels real."},{"start":233.8,"end":239.32,"text":"Manga also uses written sound effects called onomatopoeia directly on the page."},{"start":240.28,"end":243.7,"text":"A loud bang might appear as a large bold word inside the panel."},{"start":244.86,"end":250.12,"text":"To keep readers buying, manga stories are published in chapters inside weekly or monthly magazines."},{"start":251.5,"end":257.24,"text":"After enough chapters are printed, they are collected into a book called a tankōbon."},{"start":257.24,"end":264.58,"text":"A cliffhanger ending — a moment where something exciting happens right before the chapter stops — makes readers come back for the next issue."},{"start":265.62,"end":269.26,"text":"These tools work together to make manga a habit, not just a hobby."}],"words":[{"text":"These","start":0,"end":0.24},{"text":"old","start":0.24,"end":0.48},{"text":"works","start":0.48,"end":0.76},{"text":"are","start":0.76,"end":1},{"text":"manga's","start":1,"end":1.42},{"text":"early","start":1.42,"end":1.7},{"text":"illustrated","start":1.7,"end":2.2},{"text":"roots","start":2.2,"end":2.7},{"text":"Manga","start":2.7,"end":3.64},{"text":"has","start":3.64,"end":3.92},{"text":"very","start":3.92,"end":4.24},{"text":"old","start":4.24,"end":4.44},{"text":"roots","start":4.44,"end":4.72},{"text":"in","start":4.72,"end":4.92},{"text":"Japan","start":4.92,"end":5.24},{"text":"Around","start":6.08,"end":6.24},{"text":"the","start":6.24,"end":6.38},{"text":"year","start":6.38,"end":6.5},{"text":"1200","start":6.5,"end":6.96},{"text":"artists","start":7.46,"end":7.7},{"text":"drew","start":7.7,"end":8},{"text":"funny","start":8,"end":8.36},{"text":"animal","start":8.36,"end":8.64},{"text":"pictures","start":8.64,"end":9.1},{"text":"on","start":9.1,"end":9.44},{"text":"long","start":9.44,"end":9.74},{"text":"paper","start":9.74,"end":10.08},{"text":"scrolls","start":10.08,"end":10.56},{"text":"These","start":11.22,"end":11.38},{"text":"scrolls","start":11.38,"end":11.7},{"text":"are","start":11.7,"end":11.94},{"text":"called","start":11.94,"end":12.38},{"text":"Chōjū-giga","start":12.38,"end":14.1},{"text":"which","start":14.1,"end":14.3},{"text":"means","start":14.3,"end":14.74},{"text":"animal","start":14.74,"end":15.66},{"text":"caricatures","start":15.66,"end":16.34},{"text":"Frogs","start":17.54,"end":17.82},{"text":"and","start":17.82,"end":17.9},{"text":"rabbits","start"